{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":80393,"duration_api_ms":82160,"ttft_ms":30585,"ttft_stream_ms":2555,"time_to_request_ms":13,"num_turns":2,"result":"I've produced the new contract version. The key change: the blocking `DECISION:` entry for concern C2 (`decision-per-model-granularity`) is now a `DECIDED (C2):` entry recording option (a), and I made every dependent section consistent with that decision:\n\n- `contract_requirements/decision-per-model-granularity` — rewritten to `DECIDED (C2):`, stating option (a) was chosen (integer-only, model-name-keyed `RequestUsage.details`, no schema change; SCHEMA_VERSION stays 1; `harness/usage.py` out of scope) and option (b) rejected.\n- `must_not_change` — the SCHEMA_VERSION=1 invariant and the \"harness/usage.py unchanged\" invariant now cite the decision as settled rather than contingent.\n- `semantic/per-model-details` and `observable_behaviour/per-model-recorded` — reworded to reference the decided option (a).\n- `out_of_scope` — the schema-bump item now records that C2 rejected it.\n\nNo `DECISION:` entry remains. Every other section and obligation of version 001 is preserved unchanged, and I confirmed the deterministic criteria remain passable (the `release-note-typed` grep depends on the added file; the pytest criteria use count patterns that don't match `xfailed`/`xpassed`).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4db9a17d-a744-49bb-bd9f-d914a7c4ee79","total_cost_usd":0.65298875,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65205,"cache_read_input_tokens":58809,"output_tokens":6826,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65205,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":58809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6396},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45313,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.045388,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":6826,"cacheReadInputTokens":58809,"cacheCreationInputTokens":65205,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.60760075,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"tool_name":"final","arguments_json":"{\"response\":\"contract_version: 0.1.0\\nartifact_version: 1\\nwork_item: 20260908T113226\\nobservable_behaviour:\\n  - id: account-usage-recorded\\n    behaviour: \\\"A claude_account request whose CLI success envelope carries a `usage` block returns a `ModelResponse` with a populated `RequestUsage`, so `harness/usage.py` records non-zero input/output/cache_read/cache_write instead of the current all-zero record.\\\"\\n  - id: per-model-recorded\\n    behaviour: \\\"When the envelope's `modelUsage` map names a main model and any helper model, their counts are summed into the returned aggregate and the per-model breakdown is recorded as integer-only, model-name-keyed entries in `RequestUsage.details` (DECIDED C2, option (a): no schema change).\\\"\\n  - id: missing-usage-safe\\n    behaviour: \\\"A missing or partial `usage` block yields a zeroed `RequestUsage` and the request still records, rather than raising.\\\"\\n  - id: no-raw-no-secret\\n    behaviour: \\\"The recorded usage and its `details` contain only numeric counts and model names \\\\u2014 never the CLI `result` text, never any token or credential.\\\"\\n  - id: runbook-corrected\\n    behaviour: \\\"RUNBOOK.md \\\\u00a71 no longer states that the Claude CLI does not expose cache counters; it reflects that claude returns `cache_read_input_tokens`/`cache_creation_input_tokens` and per-model `modelUsage`, which the harness now records (concern C1).\\\"\\nrequired_outputs:\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: harness/claude_account_cli.py\\n    reason: \\\"Adds the pure `_request_usage(envelope)` helper and refactors `_invoke_claude` to pass `usage=` into the returned ModelResponse; the substantive change.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py\\n    reason: \\\"Per-helper coverage/enforcement file for this adapter; must gain tests for usage mapping, helper-model aggregation, no-raw/no-secret, missing-usage tolerance, and end-to-end populated usage.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: RUNBOOK.md\\n    reason: \\\"Correct the stale \\\\u00a71 sentence claiming the CLI does not expose cache counters (concern C1).\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: releases/_next/claude-account-usage.md\\n    reason: \\\"The release-notes CI gate requires exactly one new releases/_next/*.md (Type: patch) with Local deployment / Manual steps / Verification sections; the PR gate fails without it.\\\"\\npermitted_files: []\\ndeterministic:\\n  - id: full-test-suite\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The declared verification suite exits zero with no failures and no errors (pre-existing xfail/xpass unaffected).\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\n  - id: adapter-usage-tests\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The adapter tests, including the new usage-parsing tests, exit zero with no failures.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\n  - id: usage-convention-green\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The token-convention invariant (input_tokens includes cache read+write) stays green, proving the mapping obeyed it.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\n  - id: release-note-typed\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\"grep -RE '^\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\*Type:\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\* (patch|minor|major)' releases/_next/\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The added release note under releases/_next/ declares a patch/minor/major Type line, as the release-notes gate requires; the base commit has no such file so this depends on the change.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\nmust_not_change:\\n  - invariant: \\\"The genai-prices token convention enforced by harness/usage.py and tests/unit/test_usage.py: input_tokens INCLUDES cache read+write (USAGE_SONNET 1000+2000+100 => 3100). The mapping must satisfy it; neither file is edited.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"harness/usage.py contains no code change \\\\u2014 it already surfaces the four token fields and details and must merely inherit the populated RequestUsage (DECIDED C2, option (a): harness/usage.py stays out of scope).\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"LlmRequestRecord SCHEMA_VERSION (=1) and its single `model` column stay unchanged (DECIDED C2, option (a): per-model usage rides in RequestUsage.details, no schema bump).\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"The account-mode error and quota paths and `_redact_account_token` on every error string in harness/claude_account_cli.py; only usage population is added.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"The contract pin (contract/PINNED.json) and tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py; VERSION is not touched and no releases/v*.md is added (release-notes gate).\\\"\\nfailure_behaviour:\\n  - condition: \\\"The CLI success envelope has a missing or partial `usage` block.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"`_request_usage` returns zeroed usage and the request records normally, never raising (ADR-005 telemetry-never-fails posture).\\\"\\n  - condition: \\\"The `modelUsage` per-model sum disagrees with the top-level `usage` block.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The parser uses the `modelUsage` sum when present, otherwise the top-level block, and records both in `details` for auditability.\\\"\\ncompatibility:\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-005: record_run/telemetry never fails a successful run; the total-tolerant parser preserves this.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-019: the account transport records account-plan usage only and leaks no credential or token; ADR-018 remains history and is superseded by ADR-019 for the local POC provider.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-006: the cache-hit regression check remains `cache_read_tokens > 0` in the usage telemetry, now populatable on the account path.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-007: the live tier (tests/live, -m live) stays manual and never becomes a PR gate; pytest.ini deselects -m live by default.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"The release-notes CI gate (.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml job release-notes and .claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh): exactly one new releases/_next/*.md with a Type line and Local deployment / Manual steps / Verification (fenced bash) sections; VERSION untouched; no releases/v*.md added.\\\"\\ncompatibility_baselines: []\\ncontract_requirements:\\n  - id: scope-is-the-file-list\\n    requirement: \\\"The permitted change set is exactly required_outputs plus permitted_files; harness/usage.py, harness/agent.py, tests/unit/test_usage.py, docs/decisions.md and tests/live are outside scope.\\\"\\n  - id: decision-per-model-granularity\\n    requirement: \\\"DECIDED (C2): per-model (helper-model) usage is recorded as integer-only, model-name-keyed entries in RequestUsage.details with no schema change (option (a)); the rejected option (b) would have added a first-class per-model column via an LlmRequestRecord SCHEMA_VERSION bump. Consequently LlmRequestRecord SCHEMA_VERSION stays 1 and harness/usage.py stays out of scope. This contract's required_outputs, must_not_change (SCHEMA_VERSION=1 invariant), semantic per-model-details and observable_behaviour per-model-recorded are all written on option (a).\\\"\\n  - id: assumption-cli-field-names\\n    requirement: \\\"ASSUMPTION: the CLI top-level `usage` block uses Anthropic-style names (input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens) reporting input EXCLUDING cache (C1). Only cache_creation_input_tokens is confirmed by an existing repo fixture; the rest are asserted by concern C1, not pinned under work-store evidence.\\\"\\n  - id: gap-helper-model-shape\\n    requirement: \\\"GAP: the helper-model `modelUsage` entry shape is unobserved (concern C1). The parser tolerates and aggregates helper entries when present and records them in details; no captured helper sample pins their keys.\\\"\\n  - id: adr018-conflict-resolved\\n    requirement: \\\"ASSUMPTION: request.md vs ADR-018 ('Account plans expose neither per-request USD pricing nor provider cache counters through this CLI boundary') is resolved \\\\u2014 ADR-018 (Codex boundary) is superseded by ADR-019 (T1 review), so recording cache/per-model counters needs no new superseding ADR; adding one is out of scope.\\\"\\nsemantic:\\n  - id: usage-populated-per-convention\\n    criterion: \\\"A fake CLI success envelope carrying `usage` yields a ModelResponse whose RequestUsage sets cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens and output_tokens from the CLI counts and input_tokens = base_input + cache_read + cache_write; via usage.extract_request_records the LlmRequestRecord shows those non-zero values.\\\"\\n  - id: helper-model-aggregated\\n    criterion: \\\"An envelope whose `modelUsage` names a main and a helper model produces an aggregate summing both, and a per-model breakdown in RequestUsage.details keyed by model name.\\\"\\n  - id: per-model-details\\n    criterion: \\\"Per-model usage is recorded as integer-only, model-name-keyed details entries (DECIDED C2, option (a) of decision-per-model-granularity); no first-class column is added.\\\"\\n  - id: no-raw-response-no-credential\\n    criterion: \\\"Neither the RequestUsage, its details, nor the resulting LlmRequestRecord contains the CLI `result` text, any raw response body, or any token/credential \\\\u2014 only numeric counts and model names.\\\"\\n  - id: telemetry-never-fails\\n    criterion: \\\"A missing/empty/partial usage block produces zeroed usage and a recorded request without raising.\\\"\\n  - id: runbook-reflects-c1\\n    criterion: \\\"RUNBOOK.md \\\\u00a71 no longer claims the Claude CLI does not expose cache counters and states the harness now records cache and per-model usage (C1).\\\"\\nout_of_scope:\\n  - item: \\\"Reconciling tests/live/test_live_eval.py (the cache-counter skip and the `not complete` assertion) \\\\u2014 a live-tier behavioural decision, and any new live test must carry the `live` marker (PF-4).\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Enabling the account-mode cache-read assertion in the live tier; deferred pending captured helper-model/cache-read evidence.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Adding a superseding ADR to docs/decisions.md for the ADR-018 cache-counter claim (append-only log; resolved as superseded by ADR-019).\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"A first-class per-model column or LlmRequestRecord SCHEMA_VERSION bump (DECIDED C2 rejected this in favour of option (a); see decision-per-model-granularity), and any change to harness/usage.py or harness/agent.py.\\\"\\n\"}"},"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8fba8964-c9ae-44a1-b0e6-a1dfcbae7dcb"}
